From c517f13ec63eb3d2d3a9aca47c3c8b5fd7436a94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:04:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 61/69] panvk: large workgroups: give each logical invocation
 its own globals

A compute workgroup larger than the core holds is run as K copies per
hardware invocation, each region between barriers cloned K times. Only
function temporaries were cloned per copy: module-level temporaries
(SPIR-V Private, which is where DXVK keeps the D3D registers r0, r1,
...) stayed one per hardware invocation, so values crossing a barrier
were overwritten by the other copies.

Assassin's Creed IV (DXVK, a 512-invocation compute shader run as 4 x
128 on the Mali-G76) computed a loop bound from such a value after a
barrier and ran until the kernel stopped the job: the GPU hung and the
game froze. nir_lower_global_vars_to_local() now makes them function
temporaries before the copies are made. tests/lwg global-variable
variant: 49 151 of 61 440 results wrong before, 0 after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
index 871ffcb7ce6..706f4bdc039 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -1171,6 +1171,14 @@ panvk_lower_large_workgroup(nir_shader *nir, unsigned max_hw)
 
    nir_function_impl *impl = nir_shader_get_entrypoint(nir);
    nir_lower_returns_impl(impl);
+   /* Module-level temporaries (SPIR-V Private: DXVK's D3D registers r0, r1,
+    * ...) are per invocation too: made function temporaries here, they are
+    * cloned per copy below (or become SSA). Left global, the K copies of a
+    * hardware invocation shared them across the barriers, so every copy
+    * but one read another copy's values: Assassin's Creed IV's 512-
+    * invocation compute shader computed a loop bound from such a value
+    * and ran until the kernel stopped the job (lost device). */
+   nir_lower_global_vars_to_local(nir);
    nir_lower_vars_to_ssa(nir);
    /* Built-ins are still variable loads here: make them intrinsics first so
     * the invocation-position reads can be rewritten per copy. */
